{
  "format": "CNA.XnaDifferential.Corpus",
  "version": 1,
  "comment": "plans/plan_xnapipeline_parity.md XNAPP-267 (§23): the corpus of builds that are meant to go wrong. Same shape as corpus.json and driven by the same oracle, because a refusal has to be measured the same way an acceptance is. What this file adds is three fields. `class` names the failure the case is about. `expect` is what XNA actually did, taken from the recorded run and checked against it, so this manifest cannot drift away from the measurement. `mentions` is the subject both sides' diagnostics have to name -- the parameter, the missing file, the undeclared identifier -- which is the part of a message that can be compared at all: the sentences are each side's own, the subject is the content's. A case with no `mentions` is one whose two messages share no such token (a corrupt file is just corrupt), and there the outcome is the whole claim. `control` marks a row that is meant to build: a class needs a source on each side of its rule, or a refusal proves only that the route is broken.",
  "classes": {
    "MalformedSource": "The bytes are not what the extension and the importer say they are.",
    "TruncatedSource": "The bytes begin correctly and stop early.",
    "UnknownImporter": "The item names an importer no assembly defines.",
    "UnknownProcessor": "The item names a processor no assembly defines.",
    "ProcessorInputMismatch": "The importer's output type is not the processor's input type.",
    "UnknownParameter": "The item sets a processor parameter the processor has not got.",
    "UnparsableParameter": "The parameter exists and the text cannot be converted to its type.",
    "ImpossibleParameter": "The parameter's value is well-formed and cannot be honoured for this source.",
    "MissingDependency": "The source names a file beside it that is not there.",
    "CyclicReference": "The source's own reference graph does not terminate.",
    "UnsupportedTarget": "The content is valid and the target profile or platform cannot take it.",
    "BadDeclaration": "The document is well-formed and declares something that does not exist.",
    "MissingGlyph": "A character region asks for glyphs the resolved font has not got.",
    "ShaderCompileFailure": "The shader compiler rejected the source."
  },
